  "evidence": [
    "Standing user authority for cheap parallel full-owner recovery and coordinator-reviewed manual integration. Preserve bug-for-bug behavior, all mappings/spans/claims, structural discoveries and restoration obligations; no safety fixes.",
    "Selected short nonexact cohort is advisory; inspect original operands/control flow and existing TRIED history before selecting natural candidates. Whole owning-TU subjects conservatively cover collateral output, not permission for header/caller edits.",
    "Worker may edit only the owning C++ file and its dedicated new test, and run native compiler overlays/measurement using coordinator-bound actual application Release arguments. Maximum three evidence-backed spellings per function; group independent candidates into whole-TU decks rather than serial tree edits. No prolonged loop. Skip exhausted hypotheses unless genuinely new evidence changes the next action.",
    "All compilation must run in this isolated worktree under one native resource_environment lease from root recovery/resources.json, with absolute shared OPENSMACX_COMPILER_POOL and pinned OPENSMACX_IMAGE. Create Compiler only after acquiring lease, snapshot before/after inside it, no nested leases, jobs1 per prefix. Root shared RECOVERY_PARSE_CACHE_DIR is disposable memo only.",
    "Persist every successful raw object and input/request hashes in ignored storage BEFORE analysis, so a Python assertion cannot waste compiler work. Reuse retained objects for analysis; only a promising unqualified acquisition merits fresh compiles. Nonempty compare_unit trial label required; effective command argv is the prepared arguments tuple, flags empty.",
    "Coordinator owns all Git/preparation/claim publication/integration. Worker must not commit, rebase, stash, run record, hand-edit annotations/claims, change flags/headers or create ad hoc public tools. Return structural discoveries immediately for central scope expansion. No volatile casts, raw addresses, assembly, fake dispatch or artificial classes solely for matching.",
    "Cheap host tests first when semantic effects change; baseline and unchanged-replica native controls required; one meaningful changed-body control per deck. Measure every mapping in the unit from each object. Keep only supported complete implementation/quality/matching gains without historical-exact collateral loss; justified structural migration must be returned for review, not discarded automatically."
  ],
  "intent": "Bounded parallel whole-owner recovery and matching cohort with actual application compiler context.",
